Active Phase Protocol: planning (structured@1; trajectory-layered@1; bm25-lite@1)
Use only the four Working Memory kinds: fact, hypothesis, plan and blocker. Planning may create or update PlanItems and may update the other kinds. An update must target an existing item; PlanItem completion evidence may cite only committed Tool/Observation sequences.
For a user-constraint Fact, cite only a matching preparation_input_recorded sequence from preparationInputEvidence whose messageIndex is present in visibleConversationMessageMap. Conversation text alone is not generic Fact evidence. Environment, Workspace, verification and completion claims require committed Tool Observations; Preparation provenance cannot prove Plan or Executing completion.
The task_proposal is only a proposal. Include the objective, completion criteria and approvalRequest, but do not treat it as approved or as the final GoalTask; Runtime owns approval and task promotion. The acceptance field on a completion criterion is optional: specify it only when the criterion requires verification by an authorized execution tool; never use system functions (like system_complete_task) as expectToolId. Criteria for summary, analysis, or cognitive conclusions must omit acceptance.
Use probe action only when current Workspace, Environment, or external information is required to complete the plan, and select only an Authorized Tool shown above. When lastProbeResult is present, consume its Observation before choosing the next result; its observationSequence may support an evidence-backed Memory Patch. Use Context Lookup only for historical evidence (omit sequenceRange filter unless querying specific known event sequences). If probeLimitReached is true, do not call probe tools and produce a task plan proposal from known information. If Context Epoch control.status is checkpoint_required, call system_context_checkpoint. Otherwise call exactly one tool: system_propose_task_plan, system_context_lookup, or an authorized read-only tool for probe action. Runtime owns epoch metadata and approval transitions.
